# Pinyin defaults to the glossary's first reading; every polyphone states its reading here, and so does
# every bound compound and every character not yet in the glossary (on every occurrence).
# Passages follow Zhu Xi's chapter breaks: 14.18 = units 23–25, 14.19 = 26–27, 14.20 = 28–29, 14.21 = 30,
# 14.22 = 31–35, 14.23 = 36, 14.24 = 37, 14.25 = 38, 14.26 = 39–40, 14.27 = 41, 14.28 = 42, 14.29 = 43,
# 14.30 = 44–45, 14.31 = 46, 14.32 = 47, 14.33 = 48. Each stretch holds one chapter (no npas here).
# Quotation marks balance within every unit. Where a speech runs on past one of Zhu Xi's comments (14.18
# unit 25, the Master) the continuation is left unquoted, Chinese and English alike (as Books 8–13). In 14.22
# unit 34 the Duke's order that Kongzi repeats is quoted at the second level (『』, ‘’) inside his speech.
# Repeats: 14.27 (unit 41) = 8.14, tokens and English reused exactly; 14.30 (unit 44) 仁者不憂，知者不惑，勇者不懼
#   reuses the English of 9.28 line by line, in this chapter's order; 14.32 (unit 47) 不患人之不己知 reuses the
#   tokens and English of 1.16's first line; 以吾従大夫之後 (34, 35) 'because I follow at the rear of the grandees'
#   as 11.7; 管仲 Guan Zhong as 3.22; 康子 Kangzi (Ji Kangzi) as 10.11; 祝鮀 'the invocator Tuo' as 6.14;
#   王孫賈 Wangsun Jia as 3.13; 匹夫 'common man' (9.25); 孔子 'Kongzi' as Books 7–13; 曽子 'Master Zeng'.
