#   簡公 (jiǎn gōng — Duke Jian of Qi, personal name Ren 壬, killed 481 BC);
#   陳恒 (chén héng — Chen Heng, personal name of Chen Chengzi);
#   蘧伯玉 (qú bó yù — Qu Boyu: Qu Yuan 蘧瑗, grandee of Wei, Kongzi's host there);
#   曽子 (zēng zǐ — Master Zeng; the edition's form of 曾子 here, 14.28).
# New single characters needed (not yet GLOSS keys), with the sense used here:
#   糾 jiū (Jiu, a personal name; Zhu Xi 居黝反); 霸 bà ('to be head of, leader of the lords', Zhu Xi 霸與伯同，長也);
#   到 dào ('to reach, down to', 到于今); 被 pī ('to let (hair) hang loose', 被髮; Zhu Xi 皮寄反); 髮 fà ('hair of the
#   head'); 衽 rèn ('the front flap of a robe', Zhu Xi 衣衿也; 而審反); 諒 liàng ('petty good faith', Zhu Xi 小信也);
#   經 jīng ('to hang oneself', Zhu Xi 縊也); 瀆 dú ('a drain, a channel'); 僎 zhuàn (a personal name; 士免反);
#   靈 líng (Ling, a posthumous name); 圉 yǔ (Yu, a personal name, in 仲叔圉 and 孔圉); 怍 zuò ('to be ashamed',
#   Ma Rong 慙也); 沐 mù ('to wash the hair'); 討 tǎo ('to punish, to bring to account'); 蘧 qú (Qu, a surname);
#   曽 zēng (the edition's form of 曾, in 曽子); 暇 xiá ('leisure, spare time'); 逆 nì ('to go out to meet,
#   anticipate', Zhu Xi 未至而迎之); 覺 jué ('to perceive, become aware').
# Existing entries that need broadening (for the glosser): 匡 ('to set right', Zhu Xi and Ma Rong 匡正也); 微
#   ('were it not for', Zhu Xi and Ma Rong 微無也); 賜 ('bounty, a benefit received'); 臣 ('a household retainer',
